## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## FILE ORGANIZATION
##
## Single unified SKOS ConceptScheme with four top-level grouping concepts:
##
##   :ArtifactTypes           → 6 CSVLOD types → 24 specific artifacts
##   :MaturityStages          → Stage 0, 1, 2, 3
##   :GovernanceModel         → Tiers, Bodies, Activities
##   :ClassificationDimensions
##       ├── :NatureDimension    → Rules, Structures, Changes
##       ├── :FocusDimension     → Business-Focused, IT-Focused
##       ├── :ScopeDimension     → Organization-Wide, Initiative-Scoped, Project-Scoped
##       ├── :LifecycleDimension → Permanent, Long-Lived, Short-Lived
##       └── :FrequencyDimension → Essential, Common, Uncommon
##
## All concepts belong to the single scheme <.../eaonapage/tax#>.
## Faceted classification is achieved through properties on artifact types
## (eaop:artifactNature, eaop:artifactFocus, etc.) pointing to dimension
## concepts — not through separate schemes.
##
## See: W3C SKOS Primer §2.5 (concept schemes), §4.1 (collections)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


<https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#>
    a                skos:ConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel   "EA on a Page Classification"@en ;
    dcterms:description  '''Unified classification scheme for the EA on a Page framework.
Organizes EA artifacts (CSVLOD taxonomy), maturity stages, governance model,
and classification dimensions into a single navigable hierarchy with four
top-level grouping concepts.'''@en ;
    skos:hasTopConcept :ArtifactTypes, :MaturityStages, :GovernanceModel,
                       :ClassificationDimensions ;
    cc:license                    "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri    "https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "eaoptax" ;
    dcterms:creator               "Kalin Maldzhanski"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:title                      "Linked.Archi EA on a Page Taxonomy"@en ;
    dcterms:created               "2020-07-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified              "2026-06-15"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:publisher                  "Linked.Archi"@en, <https://linked.archi> ;
    bibo:status                   "draft" ;
    owl:versionInfo               "0.3.0"@en ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom           "EA on a Page (Svyatoslav Kotusev, 2017)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso                  <https://eaonapage.com/> .



## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## CSVLOD Artifact Types — Grouping Concept
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:ArtifactTypes
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "EA Artifact Types"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''The six general types of EA artifacts identified empirically by the
CSVLOD taxonomy: Considerations, Standards, Visions, Landscapes, Outlines, and
Designs. Each type is characterized by its nature (rules/structures/changes) and
focus (business/IT).'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :Considerations, :Standards, :Visions,
                      :Landscapes, :Outlines, :Designs ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## CSVLOD Types (6 artifact types under :ArtifactTypes)
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:Considerations
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Considerations"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Global conceptual rules and fundamental considerations important for business and relevant to IT. Dual EA artifacts relevant to both business leaders and architects."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Considerations represent planning decisions on how an organization needs to work
from the business and IT perspective. They are developed collaboratively by senior
business executives and architects and then used to influence all downstream
architectural decisions. Considerations can be viewed as the overarching
organizational context for information systems planning. The general purpose of
all Considerations is to help achieve the agreement on basic principles, values,
directions and aims. The proper use of Considerations leads to improved overall
conceptual consistency between business and IT.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Architecture principles, policies, business continuity requirements."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Rules ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :BusinessFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Consideration ;
.

:Standards
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Standards"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Global technical rules, standards, patterns and best practices relevant to IT systems. Not dual — relevant mostly to architects."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Standards represent mostly planning decisions on how all IT systems should be
implemented and some facts on current approaches and technologies. They are
developed collaboratively by architects and technical subject-matter experts and
used to shape the architectures of all IT initiatives. Standards can be regarded
as proven reusable means for IT systems implementation. The general purpose of
all Standards is to help achieve technical consistency, technological homogeneity
and regulatory compliance. The proper use of Standards leads to faster delivery
of new IT initiatives and reduced IT-related costs, risks and complexity.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Technology standards prescribing application platforms, database systems, integration patterns."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Rules ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :ITFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Standard ;
.

:Visions
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Visions"@en ;
    skos:definition   "High-level conceptual descriptions of an organization from the business perspective. Dual EA artifacts relevant to both business leaders and architects, often focusing on the long-term future up to 3-5 years ahead."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Visions represent mostly planning decisions on what IT should deliver to an
organization in the long run. They are developed collaboratively by senior business
executives and architects and then used to guide IT investments, identify,
prioritize and launch new IT initiatives. Visions can be considered as shared views
of an organization and its future agreed by business and IT. The general purpose
of all Visions is to help achieve the alignment between IT investments and
long-term business outcomes. The proper use of Visions leads to improved strategic
alignment and effectiveness of IT investments.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Business capability maps, target state architectures, strategic roadmaps."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Structures ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :BusinessFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :LongLived ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Vision ;
.

:Landscapes
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Landscapes"@en ;
    skos:definition   "High-level technical descriptions of the organizational IT landscape. Not dual — relevant predominantly to architects, more often focusing on the current state."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Landscapes represent mostly facts on the current IT landscape and some planning
decisions on its future evolution. They are developed and maintained by architects
and used to rationalize the IT landscape, manage the lifecycle of IT assets and
plan new IT initiatives. Landscapes can be viewed as a knowledge base of reference
materials on the IT landscape. The general purpose of all Landscapes is to help
understand, analyze and modify the structure of the IT landscape. The proper use
of Landscapes leads to increased reuse and reduced duplication of IT assets,
improved IT agility and decreased dependence on legacy IT systems.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Landscape diagrams, application inventories, infrastructure maps, IT roadmaps."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Structures ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :ITFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :LongLived ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Landscape ;
.

:Outlines
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Outlines"@en ;
    skos:definition   "High-level descriptions of separate IT initiatives understandable to business leaders. Dual EA artifacts relevant to both business executives and architects, usually focusing on the mid-term future up to 1-2 years ahead."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Outlines represent planning decisions on how approximately specific IT initiatives
should be implemented. They are developed collaboratively by architects and
business executives and then used to evaluate, approve and fund specific IT
initiatives. Outlines can be regarded essentially as benefit, time and price tags
for proposed IT initiatives. The general purpose of all Outlines is to help
estimate the overall business impact and value of proposed IT initiatives. The
proper use of Outlines leads to improved efficiency and ROI of IT investments.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Solution overviews, options assessments, initiative proposals."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Changes ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :BusinessFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :InitiativeScoped ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :ShortLived ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Outline ;
.

:Designs
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :ArtifactTypes ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Designs"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Detailed technical and functional descriptions of separate IT projects actionable for project teams. Dual EA artifacts relevant to both project teams and architects, usually focusing on the short-term future up to one year ahead."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Designs represent planning decisions on how exactly specific IT projects should be
implemented. They are developed collaboratively by architects, IT project teams
and business representatives and then used by project teams to implement IT
projects. Designs can be considered as communication interfaces between architects
and project teams. The general purpose of all Designs is to help implement
approved IT projects according to business and architectural requirements. The
proper use of Designs leads to improved overall quality of project delivery.'''@en ;
    skos:example      "Solution designs, preliminary solution designs."@en ;
    eaop:artifactNature :Changes ;
    eaop:artifactFocus :ITFocused ;
    eaop:artifactScope :ProjectScoped ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :ShortLived ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      eaop:Design ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Considerations — 5 artifacts
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:Principle
    a               skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :Considerations ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Principle"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Principles"@en ;
    skos:definition "Global high-level guidelines influencing all decision-making and planning in an organization."@en ;
    eaop:usageFrequency :Essential ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    eaop:usedInProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning ;
.

:Policy
    a               skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :Considerations ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Policy"@en ;
    skos:altLabel   "Policies"@en ;
    skos:definition "Overarching organizational norms typically of a restrictive nature providing compulsory prescriptions in certain areas."@en ;
    eaop:usageFrequency :Common ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    eaop:usedInProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning ;
.

:ConceptualDataModel
    a               skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :Considerations ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Conceptual Data Model"@en ;
    skos:definition "Abstract definitions of the main data entities critical for the business of an organization and their relationship."@en ;
    eaop:usageFrequency :Uncommon ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    eaop:usedInProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning ;
.

:AnalyticalReport
    a               skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :Considerations ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Analytical Report"@en ;
    skos:definition "Executive-level analyses of relevant technology trends and their potential impact on the business of an organization."@en ;
    eaop:usageFrequency :Uncommon ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    eaop:usedInProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning ;
.

:DirectionStatement
    a               skos:Concept, eaop:ArtifactType ;
    skos:broader    :Considerations ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Direction Statement"@en ;
    skos:definition "Conceptual messages communicating major organization-wide decisions with far-reaching consequences."@en ;
    eaop:usageFrequency :Uncommon ;
    eaop:artifactScope :OrganizationWide ;
    eaop:artifactLifecycle :Permanent ;
    eaop:usedInProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning ;
.


