## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## EA Maturity Stages
##
## Based on "EA Maturity on a Page" (Kotusev). Four stages from no architecture
## to true enterprise architecture. The model is descriptive, not prescriptive.
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:MaturityStages
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Maturity Stages"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Classification of EA practice maturity into four stages based on
empirical observation across 27+ organizations. Describes what is typically
observed at each stage, not what should be achieved in a linear progression.'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :StageZero, :StageOne, :StageTwo, :StageThree ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      <https://eaonapage.com/> ;
.

:StageZero
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:MaturityStage ;
    skos:broader      :MaturityStages ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Stage Zero — No Architecture"@en ;
    skos:altLabel     "Stage 0"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''No established EA practice. IT decisions are made ad hoc by individual
project teams without overarching governance, standards, or strategic alignment.
There are no dedicated architecture roles, no shared artifacts, and no
architecture governance bodies.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Typical characteristics: no EA artifacts in use, no architecture roles,
no governance arrangements, no strategic IT planning. IT is purely reactive.'''@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Duplicate systems and redundant technologies proliferate unchecked."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "IT investments are not aligned with business strategy."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "No shared understanding of the IT landscape across the organization."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Integration between systems is ad hoc and fragile."@en ;
.

:StageOne
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:MaturityStage ;
    skos:broader      :MaturityStages ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Stage One — IT Optimization"@en ;
    skos:altLabel     "Stage 1"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA practice focused on technology rationalization. Standards and
Landscapes are the primary artifacts. The Technology Optimization process is
established. Architecture governance is informal or limited to technology
standards compliance.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Typical artifacts: Technology Reference Models, Landscape Diagrams,
Inventories. Typical roles: enterprise architects focused on technology.
Governance: informal technology standards review.'''@en ;
    eaop:maturityStageProcess eaop:TechnologyOptimization ;
    eaop:maturityStageArtifact eaop:Standard, eaop:Landscape ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Reduced technology duplication through standards enforcement."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Shared visibility of the current IT landscape."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "More informed technology selection decisions."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "EA perceived as IT-only function with limited business engagement."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Architecture governance may be seen as bureaucratic overhead."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Difficulty demonstrating business value of EA practice."@en ;
.

:StageTwo
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:MaturityStage ;
    skos:broader      :MaturityStages ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Stage Two — Solution Delivery"@en ;
    skos:altLabel     "Stage 2"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA practice extends to guiding project delivery. Initiative Delivery
process is established alongside Technology Optimization. Outlines and Designs
are produced for major initiatives. Solution architect roles emerge. Architecture
review becomes a formal gate in the project lifecycle.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Typical artifacts: all Stage One artifacts plus Solution Overviews,
Options Assessments, Solution Designs. Typical roles: enterprise architects
and solution architects. Governance: formal architecture review board for
project-level decisions.'''@en ;
    eaop:maturityStageProcess eaop:TechnologyOptimization, eaop:InitiativeDelivery ;
    eaop:maturityStageArtifact eaop:Standard, eaop:Landscape, eaop:Outline, eaop:Design ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Improved solution quality through architecture review."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Better standards compliance in project implementations."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Reduced rework through early architecture guidance."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Reuse of proven patterns and reference architectures."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Architecture review may slow project delivery if not well-integrated."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Tension between enterprise standards and project-specific needs."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Strategic alignment still limited without business engagement."@en ;
.

:StageThree
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:MaturityStage ;
    skos:broader      :MaturityStages ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Stage Three — Enterprise Architecture"@en ;
    skos:altLabel     "Stage 3"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Full EA practice with all three processes established. Strategic Planning
is active, producing Considerations and Visions that guide investment decisions.
All six CSVLOD artifact types are in use. Architecture governance spans from
enterprise strategy to project delivery. Business leaders actively participate
in architecture-informed strategic planning.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    '''Typical artifacts: all 24 artifacts across all six CSVLOD types.
Typical roles: enterprise architects, solution architects, business leaders,
IT leaders. Governance: multi-tier governance with strategic and operational
review bodies, formal escalation paths, and governed artifact lifecycle.'''@en ;
    eaop:maturityStageProcess eaop:StrategicPlanning, eaop:TechnologyOptimization,
                              eaop:InitiativeDelivery ;
    eaop:maturityStageArtifact eaop:Consideration, eaop:Standard, eaop:Vision,
                               eaop:Landscape, eaop:Outline, eaop:Design ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "IT investments aligned with business strategy."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Business leaders actively engaged in architecture-informed planning."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Coherent technology landscape with managed evolution."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Consistent solution quality across the portfolio."@en ;
    eaop:maturityBenefit "Reduced total cost of ownership through rationalization and reuse."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Sustaining business engagement over time."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Keeping architecture artifacts current as the organization evolves."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Balancing governance rigor with organizational agility."@en ;
    eaop:maturityChallenge "Measuring and communicating the value of EA to the business."@en ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## EA Governance / Function
##
## Based on "EA Function on a Page" (Kotusev). Classifies governance
## arrangements, architecture tiers, and governance body types.
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:GovernanceModel
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Governance Model"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Classification of EA governance arrangements including architecture
tiers, governance body types, and governance activities. Based on EA Function
on a Page by Kotusev.'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :ArchitectureTiersGroup, :GovernanceBodiesGroup,
                      :ParticipantsGroup, :ProcessesGroup, :ProcessPhasesGroup,
                      :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    rdfs:seeAlso      <https://eaonapage.com/> ;
.


## ─── Architecture Tiers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:ArchitectureTiersGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Architecture Tiers"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Levels in the architecture governance hierarchy."@en ;
.

:OneTierModel
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArchitectureTier ;
    skos:broader      :ArchitectureTiersGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "One-Tier Model"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''A single EA team handles all architecture activities — strategic
planning, technology optimization, and initiative delivery. Typical in smaller
organizations or early-maturity EA practices.'''@en ;
    eaop:tierLevel    1 ;
.

:TwoTierModel
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArchitectureTier ;
    skos:broader      :ArchitectureTiersGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Two-Tier Model"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Enterprise architects handle strategic and technology artifacts
(Considerations, Visions, Standards, Landscapes) while solution architects
handle initiative-level artifacts (Outlines, Designs). The most common
governance model observed in practice.'''@en ;
    eaop:tierLevel    2 ;
.

:ThreeTierModel
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:ArchitectureTier ;
    skos:broader      :ArchitectureTiersGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Three-Tier Model"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Adds a domain or segment architecture layer between enterprise and
solution tiers. Domain architects manage domain-specific standards, landscapes,
and cross-initiative coordination. Typical in large, complex organizations.'''@en ;
    eaop:tierLevel    3 ;
.


## ─── Governance Bodies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:GovernanceBodiesGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Governance Bodies"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Types of organizational bodies that govern architecture decisions."@en ;
    skos:narrower     eaop:GovernanceBody ;
.

## ─── EA Processes and their phases ─────────────────────────────────────────

:ProcessesGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "EA Processes"@en ;
    skos:definition   "The three core processes of an EA practice."@en ;
    skos:narrower     eaop:StrategicPlanning, eaop:InitiativeDelivery, eaop:TechnologyOptimization ;
.

:ProcessPhasesGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "EA Process Phases"@en ;
    skos:definition   "The phases an initiative passes through within the core EA processes."@en ;
    skos:narrower     eaop:StrategicPlanningCycle, eaop:Initiation, eaop:Realization ;
.

## ─── Participants ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:ParticipantsGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Participants"@en ;
    skos:definition   "The stakeholders who take part in the EA practice's processes."@en ;
    skos:narrower     eaop:BusinessLeader, eaop:ITLeader, eaop:EnterpriseArchitect,
                      eaop:SolutionArchitect ;
.

:ArchitectureReviewBoard
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:GovernanceBody ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceBodiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Architecture Review Board"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''A governance body that reviews and approves architecture artifacts,
particularly Outlines and Designs, for standards compliance and strategic
alignment. Typically operates at the solution/project tier.'''@en ;
.

:SteeringCommittee
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:GovernanceBody ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceBodiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Steering Committee"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''A senior governance body that oversees strategic architecture
direction, approves Visions and Considerations, and resolves escalated
architecture decisions. Typically includes business and IT leaders.'''@en ;
.

:TechnologyCouncil
    a                 skos:Concept, eaop:GovernanceBody ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceBodiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Technology Council"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''A governance body focused on technology standards and landscape
rationalization. Reviews and approves Standards artifacts, manages the
Technology Reference Model, and governs technology lifecycle decisions.'''@en ;
.


## ─── Governance Activities ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

:GovernanceActivitiesGroup
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :GovernanceModel ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Governance Activities"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Types of governance activities in an EA practice."@en ;
.

:ReviewActivity
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader    :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Architecture Review"@en ;
    skos:definition "Review of architecture artifacts against standards, principles, and strategic direction."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso    eaop:ArchitectureReview ;
.

:ApprovalActivity
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader    :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Approval"@en ;
    skos:definition "Formal approval of an architecture artifact or initiative to proceed."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso    eaop:Approval ;
.

:AmendmentActivity
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader    :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Amendment"@en ;
    skos:definition "Modification of an approved architecture artifact to reflect changed requirements."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso    eaop:Amendment ;
.

:ExemptionActivity
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader    :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Exemption"@en ;
    skos:definition "Temporary deviation from established standards or principles for a specific initiative."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso    eaop:Exemption ;
.

:EscalationActivity
    a               skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader    :GovernanceActivitiesGroup ;
    skos:inScheme   <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Escalation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Escalation of a decision or conflict to a higher-tier governance body."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso    eaop:Escalation ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Classification Dimensions
##
## The CSVLOD taxonomy classifies artifacts along multiple independent axes.
## These are grouped under :ClassificationDimensions for navigability.
## Artifact types reference dimension values via properties (eaop:artifactNature,
## eaop:artifactFocus, eaop:artifactScope, eaop:artifactLifecycle, eaop:usageFrequency).
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:ClassificationDimensions
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Classification Dimensions"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''The independent facets used to classify EA artifacts. Each artifact
is classified along all dimensions simultaneously (post-coordinated).'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :NatureDimension, :FocusDimension, :ScopeDimension,
                      :LifecycleDimension, :FrequencyDimension ;
.


## ─── Nature (What do artifacts describe?) ──────────────────────────────────
##
## The first dimension of the CSVLOD taxonomy classifies EA artifacts based on
## what objects they describe.
##
## | Nature     | Describe                                                         | Scope                                              | Format                   | Question                                          | Lifecycle                                           | Role                                                | Purpose                                                             |
## |------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
## | Rules      | General global rules defining an organization or its divisions   | Very broad, often relate to an entire organization | Often textual            | How do we work or want to work?                   | Permanent, created once and then periodically updated | Basis for all other planning decisions              | Help achieve consistency and homogeneity of all planning decisions  |
## | Structures | High-level structures of an organization or its parts            | Broad, often cover large areas of an organization  | Usually graphical        | What approximately do we have or want to have?    | Permanent, created once and then continuously updated | High-level maps facilitating decision-making        | Help understand what changes are desirable and how to implement them |
## | Changes    | Specific proposed incremental changes to an organization         | Narrow, limited to separate IT initiatives/projects | Mix of textual/graphical | What exactly are we going to change right now?     | Temporary, created for specific purposes then discarded | Tactical plans of an organization                   | Help plan separate changes in detail                                |
##
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:NatureDimension
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ClassificationDimensions ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Nature"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Classification of EA artifacts by what objects they describe. The first
dimension of the CSVLOD taxonomy organizes all EA artifacts into rules, structures
and changes.'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :Rules, :Structures, :Changes ;
.

:Rules
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :NatureDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Rules"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA artifacts that describe general global rules defining an organization
or its divisions. Rules are permanent, created once and periodically updated. They
do not refer to specific instances but apply to all instances of a certain type.
Rules provide the basis for all other planning decisions and answer: "How do we
work or want to work?"'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    "Often represented in textual formats. Intangible and uncountable. The most stable and infrequently changing EA artifacts."@en ;
    skos:example      "Considerations (principles, policies) and Standards (technology reference models, patterns)."@en ;
.

:Structures
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :NatureDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Structures"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA artifacts that describe high-level structures of an organization or
its parts. Structures refer to specific but relatively abstract instances and
often describe relationships between them. They are permanent, created once and
continuously updated. Structures provide high-level maps facilitating
decision-making and answer: "What approximately do we have or want to have?"'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    "Usually represented in graphical formats. Tangible and countable. Change together with an organization and its plans."@en ;
    skos:example      "Visions (capability maps, target architectures) and Landscapes (application maps, inventories)."@en ;
.

:Changes
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :NatureDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Changes"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA artifacts that describe specific proposed incremental changes to
an organization — separate change initiatives or projects. Changes thoroughly
describe concrete instances with internal details. They are temporary, created
for specific purposes and then discarded. Changes represent the tactical plans
and answer: "What exactly are we going to change right now?"'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    "Usually represented in mixed textual and graphical formats. The most volatile EA artifacts with short lifespans limited to project timeframes."@en ;
    skos:example      "Outlines (solution overviews, options assessments) and Designs (solution designs, detailed specifications)."@en ;
.


## ─── Focus (How do artifacts describe objects?) ────────────────────────────
##
## The second dimension of the CSVLOD taxonomy classifies EA artifacts based on
## how they describe objects.
##
## | Focus            | Language                               | Domains                                                                             | Format                                                               | Stakeholders                       | Role                                           | Purpose                              |
## |------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
## | Business-Focused | Technology-neutral business language   | Business domain and often other relevant domains at a high level                    | Brief, intuitive, largely informal, only the most essential info     | Business leaders and architects    | Communication interfaces between business & IT | Help business leaders manage IT      |
## | IT-Focused       | Technical IT-specific language         | Applications, data, integration, infrastructure, security and sometimes business    | Can be voluminous, formal, strict notations, comprehensive details   | Architects and other IT specialists | Internal IT tools invisible to business        | Help architects organize IT          |
##
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:FocusDimension
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ClassificationDimensions ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Focus"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''Classification of EA artifacts by how they describe objects. The second
dimension of the CSVLOD taxonomy classifies all EA artifacts into business-focused
and IT-focused.'''@en ;
    skos:narrower     :BusinessFocused, :ITFocused ;
.

:BusinessFocused
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :FocusDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Business-Focused"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA artifacts that tend to be technology-neutral and use plain business
language (money, customers, capabilities, business goals). They are brief, largely
informal, use intuitive presentation formats, and contain only the most essential
information relevant to executive-level audience. Business-focused artifacts are
always dual — they serve as communication interfaces between business and IT.
All are either developed collaboratively by architects and business executives, or
at least consciously approved by business leaders.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    "Help business leaders manage IT without understanding its technical details."@en ;
.

:ITFocused
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :FocusDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "IT-Focused"@en ;
    skos:definition   '''EA artifacts that tend to be purely technical and use highly IT-specific
language (systems, applications, databases, platforms, networks). They can be
voluminous, formal, and detailed, sometimes using specialized modeling notations.
IT-focused artifacts are intended primarily for architects and other IT specialists
— used as reference materials for decision-making and project implementation within
the IT department. Essentially internal IT tools invisible to business.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote    "Help architects organize IT according to their best understanding of the business interests."@en ;
.


## ─── Scope ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:ScopeDimension
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ClassificationDimensions ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Scope"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Classification of EA artifacts by organizational scope."@en ;
    skos:narrower     :OrganizationWide, :InitiativeScoped, :ProjectScoped ;
.

:OrganizationWide
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ScopeDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Organization-Wide"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts that apply across the entire organization."@en ;
.

:InitiativeScoped
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ScopeDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Initiative-Scoped"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts scoped to a specific initiative or programme of work."@en ;
.

:ProjectScoped
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ScopeDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Project-Scoped"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts scoped to a specific delivery project."@en ;
.


## ─── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:LifecycleDimension
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ClassificationDimensions ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Lifecycle"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Classification of EA artifacts by temporal lifecycle."@en ;
    skos:narrower     :Permanent, :LongLived, :ShortLived ;
.

:Permanent
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :LifecycleDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Permanent"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts developed once and updated periodically — rarely change fundamentally."@en ;
.

:LongLived
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :LifecycleDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Long-Lived"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts maintained continuously and evolving as the organization changes."@en ;
.

:ShortLived
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :LifecycleDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Short-Lived"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Artifacts produced for a specific initiative or project, then archived."@en ;
.


## ─── Usage Frequency ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:FrequencyDimension
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :ClassificationDimensions ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Usage Frequency"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Classification of EA artifact types by how commonly they are used across organizations."@en ;
    skos:narrower     :Essential, :Common, :Uncommon ;
.

:Essential
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :FrequencyDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Essential"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Used by the majority of organizations with an EA practice."@en ;
.

:Common
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :FrequencyDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Common"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Used by 25-50% of organizations with an EA practice."@en ;
.

:Uncommon
    a                 skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader      :FrequencyDimension ;
    skos:inScheme     <https://meta.linked.archi/eaonapage/tax#> ;
    skos:prefLabel    "Uncommon"@en ;
    skos:definition   "Used by 10-25% of organizations with an EA practice."@en ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Palette grouping
##
## Linked.Archi modelling guidance, not the framework: the classification
## dimensions a palette groups element types by. The metamodel manifest points
## to it (arch:paletteGrouping).
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:PaletteGrouping
    a               skos:OrderedCollection ;
    skos:prefLabel  "Palette Grouping"@en ;
    skos:definition "The classification dimensions a palette groups element types by: the groups of the governance model — bodies, participants, processes, phases and activities — then the process types of the Architecture Processes extension, which the framework's processes specialise."@en ;
    skos:memberList ( :GovernanceModel aptax:ElementKind ) ;
.

